## Stop publishing local-only docs trees to GitHub

Context: `docs/sphinx/`, `docs/superpowers/`, and `docs/pr47-neo4j-demo/` were
git-tracked and therefore published. They stay on disk for local work but must
not sync to GitHub. Databricks DAB already excluded them from the app payload.

Changes:

1. .gitignore
   Ignore the three local-only docs trees.
2. git index (`git rm -r --cached`)
   Untrack the trees without deleting working-copy files.
3. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Point the Neo4j setup-guide link at tracked `docs/neo4j-requirements.md`.
4. docs/neo4j-requirements.md
   Drop the GitHub-facing pointer at the unpublished demo pack.
5. docs/deployment.md
   Route Neo4j secret-setup references to `docs/neo4j-requirements.md`.
6. docs/README.md
   Note that Sphinx sources are local-only.
7. .cursor/07-project-conventions.mdc
   Note that `docs/superpowers/` is gitignored.

